A number is said to be palindrome if it is the same when reversed. The below is code written to check if the entered 5 digit number is a palindrome or not.
Answer the following questions with respect to the code given below :
a)   Why is the header file “stdlib.h” included in the below program?
b)   The code has few compile time and logical errors. You are asked to fix both the errors so that we get the desired output.
      Justify your answers for each correction made in the code.

#include<stdio.h>
#include<stdlib.h>
#define MIN = 0     //Macro defined with the upper and lower limits
#define MAX = 99999
int main()
{
int num=89898,temp,rem,rev=0;
if(num<MAX || num> MIN) //To check for if the number is 5 digit for not.
{
     printf("Please enter a 5 digit number only");
     exit(0);                     //To exit from the program
}
for(;num>0;num =/10)   //To reverse a number
{
        rem=num%10;
        rev *= 10 + rem;
}
if(num = rev)               //Check if they are same
      printf("Entered Number is a Palindrome \n");
else
     printf("Not a Palindrome \n");
}

